meson: -dead_strip on darwin as the ld64 form of --gc-sections

ld_args_gc_sections is how every driver drops the shared code it does not use ("particularly relevant for Vulkan
drivers"); it only probes for --gc-sections, which ld64 does not have, so darwin builds keep everything. ld64's
equivalent is -dead_strip; Mach-O objects are already split per symbol (MH_SUBSECTIONS_VIA_SYMBOLS), so no
-ffunction-sections/-fdata-sections is needed.

libvulkan_intel.dylib (x86_64, prod8 objects; the meson build is byte-identical to relinking build-prod8's objects
with -Wl,-dead_strip): 31.7 -> 26.9 MB, __TEXT 27.8 -> 23.6 MiB, __DATA_CONST 624 -> 512 KiB, rebases 11526 -> 8950
(pages with fixups 152 -> 125), binds 349 -> 330, the optional entrypoints resolved to NULL 10954 -> 9195. Same
175 exports, same 9 initializers, same ObjC sections; the 22 entrypoint tables anv uses are identical slot by slot
(9702 NULL); the 7 dropped are the Android and vk_cmd_enqueue tables nothing references. All 865 commands resolve
the same through vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr. dlopen time is unchanged within noise (3.20 -> 3.18 ms median under
Rosetta); the gain is size and ~27 fewer dirty pages per process.

